From: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: do not tear down PMF-protected associations on unprotected auth

ap_sta_re_add() unconditionally issues a driver STA remove for the
transmitter address before re-adding the entry. On an AP MLD all links
share one netdev, so DEL_STATION removes a kernel station by MAC address
alone: an unprotected (spoofable) Authentication frame received on one
link deletes the live kernel ML entry of a client that holds an
authorized, PMF-protected association on another link, blackholing the
client despite management frame protection.

Skip the kernel remove/re-add cycle when any partner link has an
authorized WLAN_STA_MFP station for the same MAC address, mirroring the
same-BSS PMF guard in handle_auth(). The authentication exchange still
proceeds; a genuine reconnection is resolved through the SA Query
procedure, as required by IEEE 802.11 management frame protection.

Signed-off-by: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
---

--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -2172,7 +2172,32 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	/* Clear stale, unauthorized MLD state before any new association. */
 	ap_sta_remove_link_sta(hapd, sta, check_authorized);
+
+	/* All links of an AP MLD share one netdev, so the DEL_STATION issued
+	 * below removes a kernel entry by MAC address alone. If another link
+	 * still has an authorized association protected by PMF for this MAC
+	 * address, an unprotected Authentication frame received on this link
+	 * must not be allowed to tear that association down. Mirror the
+	 * same-BSS PMF guard from handle_auth() and leave the existing entry
+	 * intact; a subsequent (re)association attempt is resolved through
+	 * the SA Query procedure. */
+	if (check_authorized && hapd->conf->mld_ap && hapd->mld) {
+		struct hostapd_data *tmp_hapd;
 
+		for_each_mld_link(tmp_hapd, hapd) {
+			struct sta_info *tmp_sta;
+
+			if (tmp_hapd == hapd)
+				continue;
+
+			tmp_sta = ap_get_sta(tmp_hapd, sta->addr);
+			if (tmp_sta && tmp_sta != sta &&
+			    (tmp_sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) &&
+			    ap_sta_is_authorized(tmp_sta))
+				return 0;
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta)) {
 		u8 mld_link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
 
